<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zayed bin Khalifa Al Nahyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1840–1909</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Zayed the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zayed bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nahyan">Al Nahyan</a>, known as Zayed the Great, was ruler of Abu Dhabi from 1855 to 1909. Through war and alliances with inland tribes he made Abu Dhabi the strongest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>, and he signed the Exclusive Agreement with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1892. His descendants, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan">Sheikh Zayed</a> bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a>, have ruled Abu Dhabi since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-khalifa-al-nahyan.jpg" alt="Zayed bin Khalifa Al Nahyan" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: عبدالقادر السعدي مع تعديل بسيط في الالوان من قبلي · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%AF_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%83%D8%A8%D9%8A%D8%B1_%D8%A8%D9%86_%D8%AE%D9%84%D9%8A%D9%81%D8%A9_%D8%A2%D9%84_%D9%86%D9%87%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%86.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
